    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bufremove\n\n### Description\n\nThe bufdelete.nvim package adds two handy events:\r\n\r\n* `BDeletePre`\r\n* `BDeletePost`\r\n\r\nI'd like to add an autocommand that allows me to open Alpha.nvim when all of the buffers close. With bufdelete.nvim, this can be accomplished like this:\r\n\r\n``` lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\r\n  pattern = \"BDeletePost*\",\r\n  group = \"alpha_on_empty\",\r\n  callback = function(event)\r\n    local buffer_name = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(event.buf)\r\n    local buffer_filetype = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_option(event.buf, \"filetype\")\r\n    local is_empty = buffer_name == \"\" and buffer_filetype == \"\"\r\n\r\n    if is_empty then\r\n      vim.cmd(\"Alpha\")\r\n    end\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be awesome if mini.bufremove could also add two events, such as `MiniBufremovePre` and `MiniBufremovePost` to enable this.\r\n\r\nThank you for the great plugins!",
